.TH byssus-check 8  "byssus 0.1.0" "Byssus Manual"
.SH NAME
byssus\-check \- Check whether the configuration would be accepted by a reload, optionally with drop\-in fragments added, replaced or removed, without installing anything or signaling the daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbyssus check\fR [\fB\-\-add\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-remove\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-slave\-namespace\fR] [\fB\-\-log\-level\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Check whether the configuration would be accepted by a reload, optionally with drop\-in fragments added, replaced or removed, without installing anything or signaling the daemon.
.PP
Runs the same validation as a SIGHUP reload: parsing, ownership and modes, cross\-group rules, paths, opening every root and membership directory, watches and propagation. When run as root with a service user configured, access is checked as that user. Exits 0 if the configuration would be accepted, 1 otherwise.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-add\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Candidate drop\-in fragment, treated as installed in the drop\-in directory under its file name (replacing a fragment of that name). May be repeated
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Main configuration file [default: /etc/byssus/byssus.toml]
.TP
\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Drop\-in configuration directory [default: /etc/byssus/conf.d]
.TP
\fB\-\-remove\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
File name of an installed drop\-in fragment to leave out. May be repeated
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-slave\-namespace\fR
Treat target roots on slave mounts as acceptable (as byssusd \-\-allow\-slave\-namespace would)
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-level\fR \fI<LEVEL>\fR
Log level for diagnostics on stderr: error, warn, info, debug, trace
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: text]
Output format
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
text
.IP \(bu 2
json
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
